Package: budgetsc
Type: Package
Title: Reproducible Synthetic-Control and Bayesian Post-Estimation Pipeline for the Household Budgeting Study
Version: 0.4.11
Authors@R: person("Andre", "Bonfrer", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "andre.bonfrer@deakin.edu.au")
Description: Analysis pipeline for the digital-budgeting and financial-wellbeing
    project. A run is described by a specification (spec) with a deterministic
    identifier; runs read a processed analysis panel, build the sample for a
    chosen design (later adopters, onboarder donor pools, placebo dates,
    distress subsets), fit regularised multi-outcome synthetic controls
    (augMultiSynth), estimate heterogeneous treatment effects with Bayesian
    post-estimation (scmBayesPost), and write tidy CSV tables with HTML/LaTeX
    twins plus diagnostics (pre-trend fit, held-out gaps, placebo outcomes).
    A directory-based lock protocol lets several machines on one shared
    filesystem work through registered runs without a scheduler.
